  "findings": "Opposite leaves on upright stems, bifurcated upper flowering branches with small pink flowers. Generic dense slabs rejected. Dedicated silene staged; split petal tips and inflated calyx below25mm. Current seeds 1, 4 and 7 and every panel in the 36-seed contact sheet were visually inspected. Upright opposite-leaved stems fork into small pink flowers. The 38\u201378 cm forms show different shoot spacing and lean. Split petal tips and inflated calyces remain below the selected pitch. The Curtis illustration was supplementary; Lindsey and Slemmons photographs were the actual photographic evidence. Accepted as a coarse stylized spring source at 25 mm; user endorsement remains separate.",
